lg:DE-BFSG-s1-3-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "edaaad24bfe13c9f460d35a9c2d862f5f7492e1245717f548973e73a3d0f2b69" ;
    lgo:text """(3) This Act applies to the following services provided to consumers after 28 June 2025:
1. telecommunications services with the exception of transmission services used for the provision of machine-to-machine services;
2. the following elements of passenger transport services by air, bus, rail and ship, with the exception of urban, suburban and regional transport services, for which only the elements under letter e apply:
a) websites;
b) services provided on mobile devices, including mobile applications;
c) electronic tickets and electronic ticketing services;
d) the provision of information relating to the transport service, including real-time travel information, but in the case of information screens only if they are interactive screens located within the territory of the European Union, and
e) interactive self-service terminals located within the territory of the European Union, with the exception of terminals installed as integrated parts of vehicles, aircraft, ships and rolling stock and used to provide such passenger transport services;
3. banking services for consumers;
4. e-books and dedicated software for them, and
5. e-commerce services."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BFSG-s1-3-q1 .

lg:DE-BFSG-s14-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "c0bd7d83188c9b674095fa217f52025db10ccee6e046ed2ddd3faeeba8b08f96" ;
    lgo:text """(1) The service provider may offer or provide its service only if
1. the service meets the accessibility requirements of the ordinance to be issued under § 3(2), and
2. it has drawn up the information under Annex 3 number 1 and made that information available to the public in an accessible form; the requirements of the ordinance to be issued under § 3(2) govern how it is made available."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BFSG-s14-1-q1 .

lg:DE-BFSG-s3-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "fc0359e6d5b79caad370e6a66e4746826f53ec7acc0604d716c6e8280eb53907" ;
    lgo:text "(1) Products that an economic operator makes available on the market, and services that it offers or provides, must be accessible. Products and services are accessible if persons with disabilities can find, access and use them in the generally usual way, without particular difficulty and in principle without outside help. The specific accessibility requirements for products and services under this paragraph are laid down in the ordinance to be issued under paragraph 2."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BFSG-s3-1-q1 .

lg:DE-BFSG-s3-3-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "7fbeafa491c87f7dd92e447acb9d69fe13dd61075693e7658459eece6b8c5bf4" ;
    lgo:text "(3) Paragraph 1 does not apply to microenterprises that offer or provide services. The Federal Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs, in agreement with the Federal Ministry for Economic Affairs and Energy, shall draw up guidelines for microenterprises to make it easier for them to apply this Act. The Federal Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs may use third parties in drawing up the guidelines under sentence 2."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BFSG-s3-3-q1 .

lg:DE-BFSG-source-legalStatus-ee017f0a4a4d-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "ee017f0a4a4d9a8f0b9c388e630883a9459e5a5f6790bc403336112b6721f60f" ;
    lgo:text "Last amended by Art. 32 of the Act of 6 May 2024 (BGBl. I No. 149)"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translatedProperty lgo:legalStatus ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BFSG-source .

lg:DE-BGB-s195-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "b124d671d9c94f510ea1391e4f058d9bbe44213a09e7084f514fc0ee617bd046" ;
    lgo:text "The regular limitation period is three years."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGB-s195-q1 .

lg:DE-BGB-s199-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "3d70d4eff89c8b4ad60a59c007a4a447528beb6df6ea9f7ab486da69dcc54f7f" ;
    lgo:text """(1) Unless another start of limitation is specified, the regular limitation period begins at the end of the year in which
1. the claim arose and
2. the obligee obtains knowledge of the circumstances giving rise to the claim and the identity of the obligor, or would have obtained it without gross negligence."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGB-s199-1-q1 .

lg:DE-BGB-s305-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "f93783819689092afdaccebbef4fe2c5533a43bc2b3f978bfa5d0b7eddbf4c02" ;
    lgo:text """(2) Standard business terms become part of a contract only if the user, when the contract is concluded,
1. refers the other party to them expressly or, where an express reference is possible only with disproportionate difficulty because of the way the contract is concluded, by a clearly visible notice at the place where the contract is concluded, and
2. gives the other party the opportunity, in a reasonable manner that also takes appropriate account of a physical disability of the other party recognisable to the user, to take note of their content,
and if the other party agrees to their application."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGB-s305-2-q1 .

lg:DE-BGB-s307-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "848c37ca636906f7ae548ecf425eb77bc4111d81f734c5bfb3cf5dbb490caa52" ;
    lgo:text "(1) Provisions in standard business terms are ineffective if, contrary to the requirement of good faith, they unreasonably disadvantage the user's contractual partner. An unreasonable disadvantage may also arise from the provision not being clear and comprehensible."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGB-s307-1-q1 .

lg:DE-BGB-s309-9-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "8e0b37ecdbdb5634c1ecf49e38973ce77e694dd2652f2606c1ca5c792259a810" ;
    lgo:text """in a contractual relationship whose subject is the regular supply of goods or the regular provision of services or work by the user,
a) a term of the contract binding the other party for longer than two years,
b) a tacit extension of the contractual relationship binding the other party, unless the contractual relationship is extended only for an indefinite period and the other party is given the right to terminate the extended contractual relationship at any time with a notice period of no more than one month, or
c) a notice period, to the detriment of the other party, longer than one month before the end of the originally intended term of the contract;
this does not apply to contracts for the supply of items sold as belonging together or to insurance contracts;"""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGB-s309-9-q1 .

lg:DE-BGB-s312i-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "af40e0dfad7e7e7f144c6aa0d2f17316304258dfb98a5f326f4d875ce0596018" ;
    lgo:text """(1) If a trader uses digital services within the meaning of § 1(4) no. 1 of the Digital Services Act (DDG) for the purpose of concluding a contract for the supply of goods or the provision of services (contract in electronic commerce), the trader must
1. provide the customer with appropriate, effective and accessible technical means by which the customer can identify and correct input errors before placing the order,
2. communicate to the customer clearly and comprehensibly, in good time before the order is placed, the information specified in Article 246c of the Introductory Act to the Civil Code,
3. confirm receipt of the customer's order without undue delay by electronic means, and
4. enable the customer to retrieve the contract terms, including the standard business terms, when the contract is concluded and to store them in a reproducible form.
The order and the acknowledgement of receipt within the meaning of sentence 1 no. 3 are deemed to have been received when the parties to whom they are addressed can retrieve them under normal circumstances."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGB-s312i-1-q1 .

lg:DE-BGB-s312j-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "03cff08dbcffcbc224b15bb2423b8c3aa9b313a1fd080f068698d7f264fdf081" ;
    lgo:text "(2) In a consumer contract in electronic commerce that obliges the consumer to pay, the trader must provide the consumer with the information under Article 246a § 1(1) sentence 1 numbers 1, 5 to 8, 11a, 14 and 15 of the Introductory Act to the Civil Code clearly, comprehensibly and in a prominent manner immediately before the consumer places the order."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGB-s312j-2-q1 .

lg:DE-BGB-s312j-3-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "5e42a5a75af61021ce1bef76f5c8d2da551ab832790a7ca892e92269e35b7a09" ;
    lgo:text "(3) The trader shall design the ordering process for a contract under paragraph 2 so that, by placing the order, the consumer expressly confirms that they undertake an obligation to pay. If the order is placed by means of a button, the trader's obligation under sentence 1 is fulfilled only if the button is labelled in an easily legible manner with nothing other than the words \"zahlungspflichtig bestellen\" (order with obligation to pay) or with a corresponding unambiguous wording."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGB-s312j-3-q1 .

lg:DE-BGB-s312k-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "07f750a0bcf32d1df836f56f0dd3deb4a4f476874239c6f47825825e6836c76a" ;
    lgo:text """(1) If consumers are enabled via a website to conclude a contract in electronic commerce aimed at establishing a continuing obligation that obliges a trader to provide a service for payment, the trader has the obligations under this provision. This does not apply
1. to contracts for whose termination the law prescribes exclusively a stricter form than text form, and
2. in relation to websites concerning financial services, or to contracts for financial services."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGB-s312k-1-q1 .

lg:DE-BGB-s312k-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "f782ccde3eb34583e427423026e91c50420156a31755150d04f681941c9fd875" ;
    lgo:text """(2) The trader must ensure that the consumer can make a declaration of ordinary or extraordinary termination of a contract under subsection 1 sentence 1 that can be concluded on the website, by means of a termination button on the website. The termination button must be legibly labelled with nothing other than the words “cancel contracts here” (“Verträge hier kündigen”) or with a corresponding unambiguous wording. It must lead the consumer directly to a confirmation page that
1. asks the consumer for, and enables the consumer to give, information
a) on the type of termination and, in the case of extraordinary termination, the reason for termination,
b) on the consumer's unambiguous identification,
c) on the unambiguous designation of the contract,
d) on the time at which the termination is to end the contractual relationship,
e) on the rapid electronic transmission of the termination confirmation to the consumer, and
2. contains a confirmation button by which the consumer can make the declaration of termination and which is legibly labelled with nothing other than the words “cancel now” (“jetzt kündigen”) or with a corresponding unambiguous wording.
The buttons and the confirmation page must be permanently available and directly and easily accessible."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGB-s312k-2-q1 .

lg:DE-BGB-s356a-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "66acac8e25c09ca5b6f770275b586b7354e2a5915db211c26b78462708c723e0" ;
    lgo:text "(1) For distance contracts concluded via an online interface, the trader shall ensure that the consumer can submit a notice of withdrawal on the online interface by using a withdrawal function. The withdrawal function must be labelled in an easily legible manner with \"Vertrag widerrufen\" (withdraw from contract) or another equivalent unambiguous wording. Throughout the withdrawal period it must be continuously available on the online interface, prominently placed and easily accessible to the consumer."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGB-s356a-1-q1 .

lg:DE-BGB-s823-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "7599a813d82ab70eab7ce51a9a43561c7429fe296fc7b1c5318c9a57edf8c80c" ;
    lgo:text "(1) A person who, intentionally or negligently, unlawfully injures the life, body, health, freedom, property or another right of another person is liable to make compensation to the other party for the damage arising from this."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGB-s823-1-q1 .

lg:DE-BGB-source-legalStatus-7448dda50bbd-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "7448dda50bbda99af7a47f1175ceef2bfcd776685ce249a24b2d5ecd3b85a3fd" ;
    lgo:text "Republished by notice of 2 January 2002, BGBl. I p. 42, 2909; 2003, p. 738;"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translatedProperty lgo:legalStatus ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGB-source .

lg:DE-BGB-source-legalStatus-9b92821f64ce-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "9b92821f64cef85f78f56790cadbb393a9b115d10727f3186ab6e4b9ef15e434" ;
    lgo:text "last amended by Art. 6 of the Act of 23 July 2026 (BGBl. I No. 226)"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translatedProperty lgo:legalStatus ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
