lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-ls-a-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "e9733904dfa17071fca43db839b13347aec30f84e69dfe6c64f1ac6a2f555680" ;
    lgo:text "a) Section 7(2) No. 2 UWG, under which telephone advertising to consumers is generally permissible only with their prior express consent (so-called 'opt-in'), is compatible with Union law."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-ls-a-q1 .

lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-ls-b-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "6c4f597eb8e3873ad95ac0039d78bc4cd19d6fbf962904db97cc812555d18794" ;
    lgo:text "b) Proof of consent requires the advertiser to fully document each individual consumer's concrete declaration of consent; in the case of an electronically transmitted declaration of consent, this requires its storage and the possibility of printing it out at any time."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-ls-b-q1 .

lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-ls-c-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "26c6c588ee8fc089fe24efc03f3ab92ebece7556c9f9d22ebde56cf8e1022c29" ;
    lgo:text "c) A confirmation mail in an electronic double-opt-in procedure neither proves the consumer's consent to advertising calls nor, by itself, leads to an easing of the burden of proof in the advertiser's favour."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-ls-c-q1 .

lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-ls-d-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "fbbccbbbb403df469e8396456fb97382cdc2f127f4694213506c090d6222c7b2" ;
    lgo:text "d) If, even after confirming his e-mail address in the double-opt-in procedure, the consumer wishes to rely on not having given the consent to e-mail advertising sent under that address, he bears the burden of pleading this."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-ls-d-q1 .

lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-ls-e-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "dfbda08641f71157a1336137d2927f6b19799d063e464d210354fdda8c8e86c5" ;
    lgo:text "e) If the consumer can show that the confirmation transmitted by e-mail does not originate from him, the advertising mail was anticompetitive even if the e-mail address was obtained in a double-opt-in procedure (following BGH, judgment of 11 March 2004 - I ZR 81/01, GRUR 2004, 517 - E-Mail-Werbung I)."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-ls-e-q1 .

lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-rn30-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "38554ac9cba7db0e641db798b80a600331ddbe3bab15d82129dd610af03ffc00" ;
    lgo:text "a) The defendant bears the burden of pleading and proof for the consent (cf. BGH, judgment of 11 March 2004 - I ZR 81/01, GRUR 2004, 517, 519 = WRP 2004, 731 - E-Mail-Werbung I). It must exist concretely in the person of the person called. The appellate court was therefore right to hold that it is not enough that the defendant, on its own account, generally does not have advertising calls made unsolicited."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-rn30-q1 .

lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-rn31-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "2b5ba745378d2a148c294b36f8297915b03cd65421a38bfc0301cc78ec1a52a4" ;
    lgo:text "Proof of consent requires the advertiser to fully document each individual consumer's concrete declaration of consent. In the case of an electronically transmitted declaration of consent, this requires its storage and the possibility of printing it out at any time. Storage is readily possible and reasonable for the advertiser. Procedures in which it is unclear whether a declaration of consent actually originates from the consumer called are unsuitable for the required proof."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-rn31-q1 .

lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-rn36-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "92cffe263bc4728c15d50d07c75b87dc94e45388b8c536efb25320fe2a6236b3" ;
    lgo:text "In any event, an electronically conducted double-opt-in procedure cannot replace an actually missing consent of consumers to advertising calls."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-rn36-q1 .

lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-rn37-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "7a6f81d5912bf14417612abcf279028acb9f40003a446a2bb43dc5ef30f388ac" ;
    lgo:text "If an application to participate is received electronically, its sender can be asked by e-mail to confirm his wish to participate. Upon receipt of the requested confirmation, it may be assumed that the application actually originates from the stated e-mail address. If the consumer has confirmed by ticking a box in the application form that he agrees to receive advertising, it is in principle sufficiently documented that he expressly consented to e-mail advertising to that e-mail address (cf. LG Berlin, K & R 2007, 430, 431; LG Essen, GRUR 2009, 353, 354 with agreeing note Klinger; LG München I, K & R 2009, 824). Under the Senate's case law, the advertiser has with such a procedure sufficiently ensured that e-mail advertising is not sent on the basis of false entries (cf. BGH, GRUR 2004, 517, 519 - E-Mail-Werbung I)."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-rn37-q1 .

lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-tenor-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "f02259f2b89b3cb89fec57435188d00d21112d0d1c644b4d96c014226b939147" ;
    lgo:text "The appeal on points of law against the judgment of the 14th Civil Senate of the Higher Regional Court of Dresden of 22 September 2009 is dismissed."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-tenor-1-q1 .

lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210-title-2033f6c2021c-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "2033f6c2021cd4876eb1f13dca17cdacfe8323bcf32e163b14caf4af31a8f27d" ;
    lgo:text "Federal Court of Justice, judgment of 10 February 2011 - I ZR 164/09 (Double-opt-in procedure)"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translatedProperty eli:title ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2011-0210 .

lg:DE-BGH-2020-0528-ls-a-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "547e8860673cbabe124c082fc22cd29928a5dcba21156c63982837e7878c6474" ;
    lgo:text "a) There is no effective consent to telephone advertising within the meaning of § 7(2) no. 2, first alternative, UWG if, when giving consent, the consumer is confronted with an elaborate procedure for deselecting partner companies listed in a list, which may lead the consumer to refrain from exercising that choice and to leave the choice of advertising partners to the trader instead. If, not having read the list and without exercising the right to choose, the consumer does not know the products or services of which traders the consent covers, there is no consent for the specific case."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2020-0528-ls-a-q1 .

lg:DE-BGH-2020-0528-ls-b-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "12f913a9ec1f22862749e740ac9c7ce0ec9e8e74633c4762c4a9dab79d965efb" ;
    lgo:text "b) In view of Article 5(3), first sentence, of Directive 2002/58/EC, § 15(3), first sentence, TMG is to be interpreted in conformity with the Directive as meaning that the service provider may use cookies to create user profiles for advertising or market research only with the user's consent. A consent to be declared electronically by the user, which permits the retrieval of information stored on the user's device by means of cookies through a pre-ticked checkbox, does not satisfy this consent requirement."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2020-0528-ls-b-q1 .

lg:DE-BGH-2020-0528-title-556234141f67-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "556234141f67b1acf81f43006c91070ad381a9b994c6c45f49a9467f4d7d7804" ;
    lgo:text "Federal Court of Justice, judgment of 28 May 2020 – I ZR 7/16 (Cookie consent II)"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translatedProperty eli:title ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-BGH-2020-0528 .

lg:DE-DDG-s3-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "63395e61b916215000bef22e55598e1c8d557ca4a44fb6a01a128315fe9f8e28" ;
    lgo:text "(1) Service providers established in Germany within the meaning of § 2, and their digital services, are subject to the requirements of German law even where the digital services are offered or distributed on a business basis in another Member State within the scope of Directive 2000/31/EC and Directive 2010/13/EU, unless Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 applies directly."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-10"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-DDG-s3-1-q1 .

lg:DE-DDG-s3-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "80318fa6414b7fdfdd2620862c1698d69caef58ba76843886e2edfc2c707c3da" ;
    lgo:text "(2) The free movement of digital services offered or distributed on a business basis in Germany, within the scope of Directives 2000/31/EC and 2010/13/EU, by service providers established in another Member State is not restricted, subject to paragraphs 5 to 7."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-10"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-DDG-s3-2-q1 .

lg:DE-DDG-s33-2-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "7aef8f13fa2c31dd346570fb1b8ebb255c891ec97cd56b2fb9294aa9bde2c644" ;
    lgo:text "contrary to § 5(1), does not keep information available, or keeps it incorrectly or incompletely,"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-DDG-s33-2-1-q1 .

lg:DE-DDG-s33-6-3-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "b568a53ae11447534d35b25ec175a732d546cab29bd3242e715329688fc41815" ;
    lgo:text "in the other cases of subsection 2, with a fine of up to fifty thousand euros."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-DDG-s33-6-3-q1 .

lg:DE-DDG-s5-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "367824e95ce12941d55fda628507cca2353b858350384184fa08c93676ea77fa" ;
    lgo:text """(1) For digital services offered on a business basis, usually for remuneration, service providers shall keep the following information permanently available, easily recognisable and directly accessible:
1. the name and the address at which they are established, and for legal persons additionally the legal form, the authorised representative and, where information on the company's capital is given, the share capital and, if not all contributions payable in cash have been paid in, the total amount of outstanding contributions,
2. details that enable rapid electronic contact and direct communication with them, including the electronic mail address,
3. where the service is offered or provided in the course of an activity that requires official authorisation, details of the competent supervisory authority,
4. the commercial register or similar register in which they are entered, and the corresponding register number,
5. where the service is offered or provided in the exercise of a profession within the meaning of Article 1(d) of Council Directive 89/48/EEC of 21 December 1988 on a general system for the recognition of higher-education diplomas awarded on completion of professional education and training of at least three years' duration (OJ L 19, 24.1.1989, p. 16), or within the meaning of Article 1(f) of Council Directive 92/51/EEC of 18 June 1992 on a second general system for the recognition of professional education and training to supplement Directive 89/48/EEC (OJ L 209, 24.7.1992, p. 25; OJ L 17, 25.1.1995, p. 20), as last amended by Directive 2006/100/EC (OJ L 363, 20.12.2006, p. 141), details of
a) the chamber to which the service providers belong,
b) the statutory professional title and the state in which the professional title was conferred,
c) the designation of the professional rules and how these rules can be accessed,
6. where they hold a VAT identification number under § 27a(1), first, second or third sentence, of the Value Added Tax Act or an economic identification number under § 139c(1) of the Fiscal Code, that number,
7. for public limited companies, partnerships limited by shares and limited liability companies that are being wound up or in liquidation, a statement to that effect,
8. for providers of audiovisual media services, a statement of
a) the Member State that is, or is deemed to be, their country of establishment, and
b) the competent regulatory and supervisory authorities."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-10-31"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-DDG-s5-1-q1 .

lg:DE-DDG-s6-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "dfc775ba615a1ebd0abc36d8408e2d125b2f47033c1973496e6ccfdf8d0d501d" ;
    lgo:text """(1) In commercial communications that are digital services or parts of digital services, service providers shall at least observe that
1. commercial communications must be clearly recognisable as such,
2. the natural or legal person on whose behalf commercial communications are made must be clearly identifiable,
3. promotional offers such as discounts, premiums and gifts must be clearly recognisable as such, and the conditions for taking advantage of them must be easily accessible and stated clearly and unambiguously, and
4. prize competitions or games with an advertising character must be clearly recognisable as such, and the conditions of participation must be easily accessible and stated clearly and unambiguously."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-10-31"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-DDG-s6-1-q1 .

lg:DE-DDG-source-legalStatus-d18f1e2aac9c-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "d18f1e2aac9ca51409a8f14b72b0f0da03a7c61b519f305a0bf7e252db857f78" ;
