lg:DE-EGBGB-a246a-s1-1-9-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "f3291e7c4a64f7246b8db09ae4fcce2c039bbf9eab5b0522e3ea32314db4b4e1" ;
    lgo:text "the cost of using the means of distance communication used to conclude the contract, where the consumer is charged more than the basic cost of using that means of distance communication"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-10"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-EGBGB-a246a-s1-1-9-q1 .

lg:DE-EGBGB-a246a-s1-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "6ac30f91d2737a89cac73710b44aef2b29307b6fafcbf9c26fa2fa25fab37e00" ;
    lgo:text """(1) Under § 312d(1) of the Civil Code, the trader is obliged to provide the consumer with the following information:
1. the main characteristics of the goods or services, to the extent appropriate to the means of communication and to the goods and services,
2. its identity, for example its trading name, and the geographic address at which it is established, and, where applicable, the identity and address of the trader on whose behalf it acts,
3. its telephone number, its email address and, where applicable, other online means of communication it provides, if these enable the consumer to keep their correspondence with the trader, including its date and time, on a durable medium,
4. in addition to the information under numbers 2 and 3, the business address of the trader and, where applicable, of the trader on whose behalf it acts, to which the consumer can address any complaint, if this address differs from the address under number 2,
5. the total price of the goods or services, including all taxes and charges, or, where the nature of the goods or services is such that the price cannot reasonably be calculated in advance, the manner in which the price is calculated,
6. where applicable, the notice that the price was personalised on the basis of automated decision-making,
7. where applicable, all additional freight, delivery or postal charges and any other costs on top of the total price under number 5, or, where these costs cannot reasonably be calculated in advance, the fact that such additional costs may be payable,
8. in the case of a contract of indeterminate duration or a subscription contract, the total price; this comprises the total costs per billing period and, where such a contract is charged at a fixed rate, also the total monthly costs; where the total costs cannot reasonably be calculated in advance, the manner in which the price is calculated,
9. the cost of using the means of distance communication used to conclude the contract, where the consumer is charged more than the basic cost of using that means of distance communication,
10. the arrangements for payment, delivery and performance, including environmentally friendly delivery options where available, the date by which the trader undertakes to deliver the goods or perform the services and, where applicable, the trader's complaint handling policy,
11. the existence of a legal guarantee of conformity for goods and its main elements, including its minimum duration of two years, in a prominent manner using the harmonised notice in Annex I to Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/1960 as in force on 25 September 2025,
11a. where the producer grants the consumer a commercial guarantee of durability at no additional cost covering the entire goods for a period of more than two years and provides this information to the trader, the information that such a guarantee applies to the goods, its duration and a reference to the existence of the legal guarantee of conformity, in a prominent manner using the harmonised label in Annex II to Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/1960 as in force on 25 September 2025,
11b. a reminder of the existence of the legal guarantee of conformity for digital content and digital services,
11c. for goods with digital elements, digital content and digital services, the minimum period, expressed as a period of time or a date, for which the producer or provider supplies software updates, where the producer or provider makes this information available to the trader,
12. where applicable, the existence and conditions of after-sales assistance, after-sales services and guarantees,
13. where applicable, relevant codes of conduct within the meaning of Article 2(f) of Directive 2005/29/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 11 May 2005 concerning unfair business-to-consumer commercial practices in the internal market and amending Council Directive 84/450/EEC, Directives 97/7/EC, 98/27/EC and 2002/65/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council and Regulation (EC) No 2006/2004 of the European Parliament and of the Council (OJ L 149, 11.6.2005, p. 22; L 253, 25.9.2009, p. 18), as last amended by Directive (EU) 2019/2161 (OJ L 328, 18.12.2019, p. 7), and how copies of them can be obtained,
14. where applicable, the duration of the contract or the conditions for terminating contracts of indeterminate duration or automatically extended contracts,
15. where applicable, the minimum duration of the consumer's obligations under the contract,
16. where applicable, the fact that the trader may require the consumer to provide a deposit or other financial guarantees, and the conditions for them,
17. where applicable, the functionality of goods with digital elements or digital products, including applicable technical protection measures,
18. where applicable and relevant, the compatibility and interoperability of goods with digital elements or digital products, insofar as the trader knows or can be expected to know this information,
19. where applicable, the possibility for the consumer to use an out-of-court complaint and redress mechanism to which the trader is subject, and the conditions for access to it,
20. where applicable, the repairability score of the goods established on the basis of harmonised requirements set at Union level, and
21. where number 20 does not apply and the producer makes this information available to the trader, information on the availability, estimated cost and procedure for ordering spare parts necessary to maintain the conformity of the goods, on the availability of repair and maintenance instructions and on repair restrictions.
If the contract is concluded at a public auction, the corresponding information of the auctioneer may be provided instead of the information under sentence 1 numbers 2 to 4."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-EGBGB-a246a-s1-1-q1 .

lg:DE-EGBGB-a246a-s1-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "523c9fb586851278b998798b5aca0bcd7eddcb17273ecfc0108a81daf32b20f9" ;
    lgo:text """(2) If the consumer has a right of withdrawal under § 312g(1) of the Civil Code, the trader is obliged to inform the consumer
1. of the conditions, time limits and procedure for exercising the right of withdrawal under § 355(1) of the Civil Code and of the model withdrawal form in Annex 2, and, where applicable, of the existence and placement of the withdrawal function under § 356a of the Civil Code,
2. where applicable, that the consumer has to bear the cost of returning the goods in the event of withdrawal and, for distance contracts, additionally of the cost of returning the goods if, by their nature, they cannot normally be returned by post, and
3. that, if the consumer exercises the right of withdrawal after having expressly requested the trader to begin performance before the end of the withdrawal period, the consumer owes the trader a reasonable amount under § 357a(2) of the Civil Code
a) for services provided up to the withdrawal for which the contract provides payment of a price, or
b) for supplies of water, gas or electricity not in a limited volume or set quantity, or of district heating, made up to the withdrawal.
The trader may fulfil these information obligations by transmitting, in text form, the model withdrawal notice in Annex 1, correctly completed."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-EGBGB-a246a-s1-2-q1 .

lg:DE-EGBGB-a246a-s1-3-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "f2281d0775b4ae68c8dbbfcaa72570ac16e09d7d6a8603ceb160cdbbac83907d" ;
    lgo:text """(3) The trader must also inform the consumer if
1. the consumer has no right of withdrawal under § 312g(2) numbers 1, 2, 5 and 7 to 13 of the Civil Code, that the consumer cannot withdraw their declaration of intent, or
2. the consumer's right of withdrawal may expire early under § 312g(2) numbers 3, 4 and 6 and § 356(5) and (6) of the Civil Code, of the circumstances under which the consumer loses a right of withdrawal that initially existed."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-EGBGB-a246a-s1-3-q1 .

lg:DE-EGBGB-a246c-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "d313fe73a00e2fdcf0d42889ac45c27779ec5509f8ef5332648aa20547268145" ;
    lgo:text """In contracts in electronic commerce, the trader must inform the customer
1. about the individual technical steps leading to the conclusion of the contract,
2. whether the text of the contract will be stored by the trader after the contract is concluded and whether it will be accessible to the customer,
3. how the customer can identify and correct input errors before making the contractual declaration with the technical means provided under § 312i(1) sentence 1 no. 1 of the Civil Code,
4. about the languages available for concluding the contract, and
5. about all relevant codes of conduct to which the trader submits, and about the possibility of electronic access to these rules."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-EGBGB-a246c-q1 .

