lg:DE-JMStV-s5-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "854d6412336910b42177b6f92d1461873bd84d62ddde911fe2d4beb8027f892d" ;
    lgo:text """(1) Where providers distribute or make accessible offers that are likely to impair the development of children or adolescents into self-reliant and socially competent personalities, they must ensure that children or adolescents of the age groups concerned do not normally perceive them. In assessing the impairment of development, circumstances of the respective use of the medium that lie outside the effect of the media content may also be taken into account if they are a permanent part of the medium and justify a different overall assessment; these include in particular risks to the personal integrity of children and adolescents that are to be classified as significant on the basis of a concrete risk prognosis, in particular risks from communication and contact functions, from purchase functions, from gambling-like mechanisms, from mechanisms promoting excessive media use, from the transfer of inventory and usage data to third parties without consent, and from purchase appeals not appropriate to the age, in particular through advertising references to other media. The age groups are:
1. without age restriction,
2. from 6 years,
3. from 12 years,
4. from 16 years,
5. from 18 years."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-JMStV-s5-1-q1 .

lg:DE-JMStV-s7-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "209fbe76e619d79e462ce7faea4434067ee7ef4d3c36bc7f37b5d36b683d0711" ;
    lgo:text "(1) Anyone who broadcasts licensed television across the Länder shall appoint a youth protection officer. The same applies to commercial providers of television services not requiring a licence under § 54 of the Interstate Media Treaty or of generally accessible telemedia if the offers contain content that impairs development or is harmful to minors. The provider shall keep essential information about the youth protection officer easily recognisable, directly accessible and permanently available. It must include in particular the name and details enabling rapid electronic contact."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-JMStV-s7-1-q1 .

lg:DE-JMStV-s7-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "d832e7f7d30e598221d2c8060066511052fbe96541e8c706d7bbe62fe1dd1bb5" ;
    lgo:text "(2) Providers of telemedia with fewer than 50 employees or with demonstrably fewer than ten million visits per month on average over a year, and broadcasters whose television is not distributed nationwide, may refrain from the appointment if they join a voluntary self-regulation body, oblige it to perform the tasks of the youth protection officer and involve and inform it in accordance with paragraph 3."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-JMStV-s7-2-q1 .

lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120-p12-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "b7091463a7964661db0b19abe78f1cd8197d5f05762e2c619fe3fc978e5cfa24" ;
    lgo:text "12 The claimant has a claim for damages under Article 82(1) GDPR. Under recital 146, sentence 3, the concept of damage within the meaning of Article 82 GDPR is to be interpreted broadly. The interpretation should fully reflect the objectives of this Regulation, including the objective of sanction and prevention (BeckOK Datenschutzrecht, Wolff/Brink, 38th edition, Article 82 GDPR, para. 24). Under Article 82(1) GDPR, non-material damage is also sufficient. Whether a threshold of significance must be reached or exceeded, and so-called trivial damage excluded, is disputed (cf. BVerfG NJW 2021, 1005, para. 20 with further references; Kohn ZD 2019, 498 (501); Paal MMR 2020, 14 (16)), but can be left open in the present case. The defendant admits that, before modifying its website, it transmitted the claimant's IP address to Google when the claimant visited its website. The IP address was therefore transmitted more than once. The associated interference with the claimant's general right of personality is so significant, in view of the claimant's loss of control over a personal datum to Google, a company known to collect data about its users, and the individual discomfort the claimant thereby felt, that a claim for damages is justified."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120-p12-q1 .

lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120-p5-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "1db0aa31af69465ac16e8936dd2da4f89fd2a57203d71a8a7fbe76c630cec360" ;
    lgo:text "5 For a website operator, the dynamic IP address is personal data, because the website operator abstractly has legal means which could reasonably be used to have the person concerned identified from the stored IP addresses with the help of third parties, namely the competent authority and the internet access provider (BGH, judgment of 16.05.2017 – VI ZR 135/13). It suffices that the defendant has the abstract possibility of identifying the persons behind the IP address. Whether the defendant or Google has the concrete possibility of linking the IP address to the claimant is irrelevant."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120-p5-q1 .

lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120-p7-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "d05d53595b99f51d9ca544d65601980613d0230484b7de96089c1f753c0ae83e" ;
    lgo:text "7 The automatic transmission of the IP address by the defendant to Google was an interference with the claimant's general right of personality that was inadmissible under data protection law, since it is undisputed that the claimant did not consent to this interference under § 13(2) TMG (old version) or Article 6(1)(a) GDPR."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120-p7-q1 .

lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120-p8-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "6bd7e743b793cc7b6a4fbe55479083c6e9278b30ea9c6eb148923e0a1cdbd414" ;
    lgo:text "8 3. Nor is there any justification for the interference with the general right of personality. There is no legitimate interest of the defendant within the meaning of Article 6(1)(f) GDPR, as it claimed, because the defendant can also use Google Fonts without a connection to a Google server being established when the website is accessed and without the IP address of the website's users being transmitted to Google."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120-p8-q1 .

lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120-tenor-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "6c403ea1b4c281013abd96fe16efdaf84c4d6d95ed7abb368ee839cd44eba04c" ;
    lgo:text "1. The defendant is ordered, on pain of a coercive fine of up to €250,000.00 to be set for each case of infringement, alternatively coercive detention, or coercive detention of up to six months, to refrain from disclosing the claimant's IP address to the provider of the font Google (Google Fonts) by providing that font when the claimant accesses a website operated by the defendant."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120-tenor-1-q1 .

lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120-tenor-3-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "287f6f04b9f14a7f2a5315baa07de4789f3dea38cf41fd9bc5bbe173e851d9f9" ;
    lgo:text "3. The defendant is ordered to pay the claimant €100.00 plus interest at 5 percentage points above the base rate since 28.01.2021."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120-tenor-3-q1 .

lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120-title-c449f241d356-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "c449f241d356d587f4f7d8d3c3da3bece8143003a054abc88e1e6d1c4280183d" ;
    lgo:text "Regional Court of Munich I, final judgment of 20 January 2022 – 3 O 17493/20"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translatedProperty eli:title ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGM-2022-0120 .

lg:DE-LGM-2023-0330-p26-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "3c50451e1c3aa58cc440ca126fb4e09824095f63eece52d29b90e30eac556117" ;
    lgo:text "26 a) As a starting point, the court still shares the defendant's view that if the dynamic embedding of Google Fonts breaches the GDPR, and his IP address is transmitted to Google in the USA without a compelling technical reason and without his consent, this may constitute an infringement of the right to informational self-determination."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGM-2023-0330-p26-q1 .

lg:DE-LGM-2023-0330-p35-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "a807677810e0ce600f528f047bfededfb1a30bea13521605c21bc6b477a65072" ;
    lgo:text "35 1. The requirements of a claim under Article 82 GDPR are not met in the first place. Such a claim requires damage, possibly non-material, suffered by the claimant. Obviously there was no such damage here. Case law is divided on the extent to which feelings of fear or unease are sufficient in themselves to establish a claim for damages under Article 82 GDPR. That question does not matter here, however, because the defendant cannot actually have had such feelings, given the use of an automated program: someone who does not even know which websites are visited “in his name” cannot have any individual thoughts about the inconvenience that the transmission of his IP address might cause him."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGM-2023-0330-p35-q1 .

lg:DE-LGM-2023-0330-p36-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "e705c337c921842b96efc43b249024d519496e927bdbaf63ea27df1df3e06300" ;
    lgo:text "36 2. Moreover, any claim for damages that might nevertheless exist under Article 82 GDPR, § 823(1) BGB or any other legal basis would also be excluded as an abuse of rights, § 242 BGB. The defendant deliberately had the crawler visit websites precisely in order to establish alleged infringements of his general right of personality. It is not, however, the meaning and purpose of the general right of personality or of the data protection requirements of the GDPR to provide persons with a source of income on account of alleged infringements of their general right of personality. Anyone who deliberately provokes an infringement of his right of personality in order to derive claims from it afterwards acts against the prohibition of self-contradictory conduct."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGM-2023-0330-p36-q1 .

lg:DE-LGM-2023-0330-tenor-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "327bf7dfa725a9c5ab994125c5d53e0658e016f583dfafa4f68336bec15264e7" ;
    lgo:text "2. It is declared that the defendant has no claim against the claimant to payment of compensation for pain and suffering on account of the embedding of Google fonts on the website…, as asserted in the defendant's letter to the claimant of 20.10.2022."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGM-2023-0330-tenor-2-q1 .

lg:DE-LGM-2023-0330-title-654be4bae02d-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "654be4bae02d88cb0473687bda737860d778a176c868482789f2dee36b4c38d9" ;
    lgo:text "Regional Court of Munich I, final judgment of 30 March 2023 – 4 O 13063/22"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translatedProperty eli:title ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGM-2023-0330 .

lg:DE-LGST-2021-0512-ls-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "fc0ef764e97bcc86b4b5573d6f618e5c592409fdfb5aa1f959d7484f2446386b" ;
    lgo:text "Where a newsletter confirmation e-mail sent as part of a double-opt-in procedure contains advertising content beyond the mere request for confirmation — by the use of a logo and the phrases 'Welcome to XXX' and 'Hast du Fragen zum Newsletter? Kontaktiere uns über: info@XXX.de' — it constitutes an unlawful interference with an established and operating business."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGST-2021-0512-ls-q1 .

lg:DE-LGST-2021-0512-rn16-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "63fd5137e22da456fee8de1e83166ce6b2d72400842380528fae872439fb55d7" ;
    lgo:text "The e-mail in dispute is therefore permissible insofar as it requests confirmation of a registration on the defendant's website. However, because the e-mail has advertising content going beyond the mere request for confirmation — by the use of the logo and the phrases 'Welcome to ZzZzZzZzZ' and 'Hast du Fragen zum Newsletter? Kontaktiere uns über: info@ZzZzZzZzZ.de' — it constitutes an unlawful interference with the defendant's established and operating business."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGST-2021-0512-rn16-q1 .

lg:DE-LGST-2021-0512-rn18-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "072b52ca2a0496be96d9219f98002e16404a694fcfabadd7e4722a986bd5ff86" ;
    lgo:text "The logo and the inviting slogan 'Welcome to ZzZzZzZzZ' are capable, unlike a mere indication of the sender, of making the brand 'ZzZzZzZzZ' memorably noticeable and of generating sales-promoting customer interest. The defendant's managing director indirectly confirmed this in the personal hearing by stating that omitting the logo and the slogan 'Welcome to ZzZzZzZzZ' had reduced the demand for the newsletters. But the addition 'Hast Du Fragen zum Newsletter? Kontaktiere uns über info@ZzZzZzZzZ.de' also works indirectly sales-promoting, because it offers a service aimed at acquiring customers."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGST-2021-0512-rn18-q1 .

lg:DE-LGST-2021-0512-tenor-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "89f3eb3d4fad0b18738efc3238738da800ad9cbe666d7ecb561cf68772788c40" ;
    lgo:text "The defendant, on penalty of a coercive fine to be set by the court for each case of default and, where it cannot be enforced, of a coercive detention or a coercive detention of up to six months, to be served on its managing director (coercive fine up to EUR 250,000.00 in each case, coercive detention up to two years in total), is ordered to refrain from sending or having sent advertising letters by e-mail to the claimant, in particular for the purpose of establishing a business relationship, without the claimant having previously expressly consented to the sending."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGST-2021-0512-tenor-1-q1 .

lg:DE-LGST-2021-0512-tenor-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "9be6335bd4dab10d464e2bcf459bc2295b3e556e90d01a5e56d0047fd1a54795" ;
    lgo:text "The defendant is ordered to pay the claimant EUR 179.27 plus 5 percentage points interest above the base rate since 18 June 2020."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGST-2021-0512-tenor-2-q1 .

lg:DE-LGST-2021-0512-title-1666ce386aa1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "1666ce386aa1832202aa968532dd3fc0367c8a7cdd124a68d4f7f430e91d41aa" ;
    lgo:text "Regional Court of Stendal, judgment of 12 May 2021 - 22 S 87/20 (advertising in the confirmation e-mail)"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translatedProperty eli:title ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-LGST-2021-0512 .

lg:DE-MStV-s18-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "b19ce8b8d13760f113df0c70289d05a2ad03b41b7040412aba2810b0b17e579a" ;
    lgo:text """(1) Providers of telemedia that do not serve exclusively personal or family purposes shall keep the following information easily recognisable, directly accessible and permanently available:
1. name and address and
2. for legal persons, also the name and address of the authorised representative."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-10-31"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-MStV-s18-1-q1 .

lg:DE-MStV-s18-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "6cc2aa103f4c626e90b23c31c85261a154c5221d0776780c9dffb753104b555d" ;
    lgo:text """(2) Providers of telemedia with journalistic-editorial offerings, in which in particular the content of periodical printed matter is reproduced in whole or in part in text or images, shall, in addition to the information required under §§ 5 and 6 of the Digital Services Act, name a responsible person, stating that person's name and address. If several responsible persons are named, it must be made clear for which part of the service each named person is responsible. Only a person may be named as responsible person who
1. is permanently resident in Germany,
2. has not lost the capacity to hold public office by court decision,
3. has unlimited legal capacity and
4. can be prosecuted without restriction.
Sentence 3 nos. 3 and 4 does not apply to young persons responsible for telemedia intended for young persons."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-10-31"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-MStV-s18-2-q1 .

lg:DE-OLGK-2024-0119-p46-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "9660dddd45e53ed33aa3e6fd58d7cad81c3d5087ebc9e0d6e12484a9d3c5812d" ;
    lgo:text "The amended application is also sufficiently definite. The demand for an “equivalent” option to reject raises no concerns in that regard. The concept of equivalence is to be understood in the sense of § 25(1) TTDSG. Accordingly, the refusal, like the consent, must be based on clear and comprehensive information."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "SWE-2" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-OLGK-2024-0119-p46-q1 .

lg:DE-OLGK-2024-0119-p51-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "7e49a076f06bacfd6db2a08c199d71e396a13377f417909a69c101167618e549" ;
    lgo:text "With a cookie banner designed as in the specific violation alleged by the claimant, the consumer is offered an equivalent option to reject — one based on clear and comprehensive information — neither on the first nor on the second level, which is why he is, as the Regional Court correctly held, steered towards giving consent and deterred from refusing the cookies, so that the consent given cannot be regarded as voluntary and adequately informed within the meaning of § 25(1) TTDSG, Article 4(11) GDPR. The first level contains no option at all for the consumer to refuse. He can reach the second level only via the “Settings” button. There the consumer then has the choice between the button “Accept all” and the button “Save”. As the Regional Court correctly held, the average user cannot work out which function actually lies behind each button or which button now actually lets him reject the cookies. The defendant itself repeatedly stated in the first instance that the consumer must have a genuine choice. That is precisely not the case with the cookie-banner design shown here."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "SWE-2" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-OLGK-2024-0119-p51-q1 .

lg:DE-OLGK-2024-0119-p54-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "d6799c641d4cb201b636cd9ccfc2ccda34cf8acecc60394d4efc9f5b0a713b54" ;
    lgo:text "This sufficiently definite application also succeeds on the merits. The design of the cookie banner with the linked button “Accept &amp; close X” in the top right-hand corner breaches the principles of transparency and voluntariness of consent and makes it invalid. The Regional Court's correct reasoning can be invoked again here. Users know the “X” symbol as a way to close a window, not as a way to consent to the website operator's use of cookies and other technologies. The average user will not be aware that this declares consent. It is true that “Accept &amp; close” stands immediately next to the “X” symbol. But linking these two functions is misleading and non-transparent for users. It is also not readily apparent to users that “Accept &amp; close” and the “X” symbol are one and the same button. Against this background, consent given by means of the “X” symbol can be regarded neither as unambiguous or clearly affirmative, nor as voluntary within the meaning of § 25(1) TTDSG, Article 4(11) GDPR."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "SWE-2" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-OLGK-2024-0119-p54-q1 .

lg:DE-OLGK-2024-0119-tenor-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "b6a1fe86bd0203830a14f542d74f59ccffb0a08e8e86de6b3f141326cbc42395" ;
    lgo:text "1. The defendant is ordered, on pain of a coercive fine of up to €250,000.00 to be set for each case of infringement, alternatively coercive detention, or coercive detention of up to six months, the coercive detention to be enforced against its respective legal representative and not to exceed two years in total, to refrain, in the course of commercial practices towards consumers in telemedia, from asking consumers by means of forms (cookie banners) to give a declaration of consent in order to store information on the user's terminal equipment, or to access information already stored in the users' terminal equipment, for purposes of advertising and/or market research, where the storage or access is not strictly necessary for the operation of the telemedium,"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-OLGK-2024-0119-tenor-1-q1 .

lg:DE-PAngV-s11-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "9fc2968a67054a135e4bca14e35110ae024256ed21182581dd4b01e5f0b88c8e" ;
    lgo:text "(1) Anyone obliged to state a total price shall, in every announcement of a price reduction for goods, state to consumers the lowest total price it applied to consumers within the last 30 days before applying the price reduction."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-PAngV-s11-1-q1 .

lg:DE-PAngV-s3-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "c4eaa314269ec4a4e992993c8f1c4b52130938bb38c6cff850ebea8d7136b834" ;
    lgo:text "(1) Any trader who offers goods or services to consumers, or who, as a provider of goods or services, advertises to consumers stating prices, shall state the total prices."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-PAngV-s3-1-q1 .

lg:DE-PAngV-s4-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "0141103f41fa455c73e31e4f3f746deab356b2cf5c787aa7eff9b89119c905f4" ;
    lgo:text "(1) Any trader who offers consumers goods in prepackages, open packages or as sales units without packaging by weight, volume, length or area, or who, as a provider of such goods, advertises to consumers stating prices, shall state the unit price, in addition to the total price, unambiguously, clearly recognisably and legibly. The unit price need not be stated if it is identical to the total price."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-PAngV-s4-1-q1 .

