lg:DE-UWG-anhang-23b-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "a1e89bd97ad3e7bad1214b79aa4940221693b51b0969f577a23b9da52bfa0a65" ;
    lgo:text "Misleading about the authenticity of consumer reviews: stating that reviews of goods or services come from consumers who actually purchased or used them, without having taken reasonable and proportionate steps to check whether the reviews actually come from such consumers;"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-UWG-anhang-23b-q1 .

lg:DE-UWG-anhang-23c-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "0a3691b63dde4528a347d2639ce723b087b49383a6cafb331eddf8366e901e0b" ;
    lgo:text "Fake consumer reviews: submitting or commissioning fake reviews or endorsements by consumers, and misrepresenting reviews or endorsements by consumers in social media, for the purpose of sales promotion;"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-UWG-anhang-23c-q1 .

lg:DE-UWG-s11-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "b98f825c0f400d07cecc7e872e6ced466846d38257b5dd601fd05c0ca57ccff0" ;
    lgo:text "(1) Claims under sections 8, 9(1) and 13(3) become time-barred after six months, and the claim under section 9(2), first sentence becomes time-barred after one year."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "swe-2-high" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-UWG-s11-1-q1 .

lg:DE-UWG-s3a-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "0e430d516a8f35e2d547ea2eca686b04006909e173e0baccb33fd61bfe597cd0" ;
    lgo:text "A person acts unfairly who infringes a statutory provision that is also intended to regulate market conduct in the interest of market participants, where the infringement is liable to appreciably harm the interests of consumers, other market participants or competitors."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-10-31"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-UWG-s3a-q1 .

lg:DE-UWG-s5a-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "25e43291704b2866f72d30e396b8460cdbc7897b7dce147fdee4e64babd5cfeb" ;
    lgo:text """(1) A person also acts unfairly who misleads a consumer or other market participant by withholding material information
1. that the consumer or other market participant needs, according to the circumstances, to take an informed transactional decision, and
2. whose withholding is liable to cause the consumer or other market participant to take a transactional decision that they would not otherwise have taken."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-10-31"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-UWG-s5a-1-q1 .

lg:DE-UWG-s5b-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "5acb8a3cbbd77958d03b401039ac4894e32fea926bedd0f32c2d5bba03a35e1f" ;
    lgo:text """(1) If goods or services are offered with reference to their characteristics and price, in a manner appropriate to the means of communication used, such that an average consumer can conclude the transaction, the following information is deemed material within the meaning of § 5a(1), unless it is already apparent from the circumstances:
1. all main characteristics of the goods or services, to the extent appropriate to the goods or services and the means of communication used,
2. the identity and address of the trader and, where applicable, the identity and address of the trader on whose behalf it acts,
3. the total price or, where the nature of the goods or services means that the price cannot be calculated in advance, the manner in which the price is calculated, and where applicable all additional freight, delivery and postal charges or, where these charges cannot be calculated in advance, the fact that such additional charges may be payable,
4. arrangements for payment, delivery and performance, where they depart from the requirements of professional diligence,
5. the existence of a right of withdrawal or cancellation, and
6. for goods or services offered on an online marketplace, whether the provider of the goods or services is a trader, according to its own declaration to the operator of the online marketplace."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-10-31"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-UWG-s5b-1-q1 .

lg:DE-UWG-s7-2-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "f96f7606a424f85522f23345ebe62ef26a94e7228d394b828680e4132cbe98c5" ;
    lgo:text "1. when advertising by telephone call to a consumer without that consumer's prior express consent, or to another market participant without at least their presumed consent,"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-UWG-s7-2-1-q1 .

lg:DE-UWG-s7-2-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "e95befa35fe62b477393fb93846c941b3161bdbe407c972c8b15a27db25d498f" ;
    lgo:text "2. when advertising using an automated calling machine, a fax machine or electronic mail, without the addressee's prior express consent, or"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-UWG-s7-2-2-q1 .

lg:DE-UWG-s7-2-3-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "797448304e454c44c675992d24fcb7f3673521a3b3ca00d771b68dd82650122d" ;
    lgo:text """3. when advertising by means of a message
a) where the identity of the sender on whose behalf the message is transmitted is disguised or concealed, or
b) where § 6(1) of the Digital Services Act is breached or the recipient is invited to visit a website that breaches that provision, or
c) where no valid address exists to which the recipient can send a request to cease such messages, without incurring costs other than the transmission costs at the basic rates."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-UWG-s7-2-3-q1 .

lg:DE-UWG-s7-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "a1a9831384f50aa249f4b608432d6cd8778999b1b317b7646f90d9af67e0a276" ;
    lgo:text """(2) An unreasonable nuisance is always to be assumed
1. in the case of advertising by telephone call to a consumer without the consumer's prior express consent, or to another market participant without at least that participant's presumed consent,
2. in the case of advertising using an automated calling machine, a fax machine or electronic mail without the prior express consent of the addressee, or
3. in the case of advertising with a message
a) in which the identity of the sender on whose behalf the message is transmitted is disguised or concealed, or
b) which infringes § 6(1) of the Digital Services Act (Germany) or in which the recipient is asked to visit a website that infringes that provision, or
c) for which there is no valid address to which the recipient can send a request to stop such messages without incurring costs other than the transmission costs at basic rates."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-UWG-s7-2-q1 .

lg:DE-UWG-s7-3-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "22934c6871b1ffadc7c4405703d1709c5d99a7580784030fe1f96aa48e9747fe" ;
    lgo:text """(3) By way of derogation from paragraph 2 number 2, advertising by electronic mail is not to be considered an unreasonable nuisance if
1. a trader has obtained the customer's electronic mail address from the customer in connection with the sale of goods or a service,
2. the trader uses the address for direct marketing of its own similar goods or services,
3. the customer has not objected to this use, and
4. when the address is collected and each time it is used, the customer is clearly and unambiguously informed that they may object to the use at any time without incurring costs other than the transmission costs at basic rates."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-02"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:DE-UWG-s7-3-q1 .

lg:DE-UWG-source-legalStatus-0a5eb3944ee7-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "0a5eb3944ee778368cefc286a5937550b1efd811b7caf7d26ef4c6d552254db1" ;
    lgo:text "Republished in a new version by notice of 3 March 2010 (BGBl. I p. 254);"@en ;
